{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:riemannian-density","title":"prop:riemannian-density","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":2087,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#prop:riemannian-density","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-density]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-density-pointwise]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:density-smooth]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:density-transformation-law]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:density-value-one]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:density-uniqueness-pointwise]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:density-positive]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:existence-orthonormal-frames]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"prop:riemannian-density","line":3346,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[The Riemannian Density]\\label{prop:riemannian-density}\\dcref{ch2:2.44}\n\n\\uses{def:smooth-density, def:riemannian-density-pointwise, prop:density-smooth, prop:density-transformation-law, prop:density-value-one, prop:density-uniqueness-pointwise, prop:density-positive, prop:existence-orthonormal-frames}\n\n\n\n\nEvery Riemannian manifold has a unique smooth positive density $\\mu$ satisfying\n\\begin{equation}\n\\mu(E_1,\\ldots,E_n)=1 \\tag{2.18}\n\\end{equation}\nfor every local orthonormal frame $(E_i)$.\n\\end{proposition}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{def:riemannian-density-pointwise,prop:density-smooth,prop:density-transformation-law,prop:density-value-one,prop:density-uniqueness-pointwise,prop:density-positive,prop:existence-orthonormal-frames}\n\\sketch Take the family of Definition \\ref{def:riemannian-density-pointwise}; Proposition \\ref{prop:density-transformation-law} makes each fibre a density and Proposition \\ref{prop:density-smooth} makes the family smooth. Proposition \\ref{prop:density-value-one} gives (2.18) and positivity. For uniqueness, evaluate any competing density on a local orthonormal frame and apply Proposition \\ref{prop:density-uniqueness-pointwise} fibrewise.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[The Riemannian Density]<span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a7269656d616e6e69616e2d64656e73697479\"></span><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch2:2.44</span></span><p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Asmooth-density\">↗ def:smooth-density</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ariemannian-density-pointwise\">↗ def:riemannian-density-pointwise</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Adensity-smooth\">↗ prop:density-smooth</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Adensity-transformation-law\">↗ prop:density-transformation-law</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Adensity-value-one\">↗ prop:density-value-one</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Adensity-uniqueness-pointwise\">↗ prop:density-uniqueness-pointwise</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Adensity-positive\">↗ prop:density-positive</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Aexistence-orthonormal-frames\">↗ prop:existence-orthonormal-frames</a> <p></p>Every Riemannian manifold has a unique smooth positive density <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\mu $\">$\\mu $</span> satisfying <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\begin{equation}  \\mu (E_1,\\ldots ,E_n)=1 \\tag {2.18} \\end{equation}\">\\begin{equation}  \\mu (E_1,\\ldots ,E_n)=1 \\tag {2.18} \\end{equation}</span> for every local orthonormal frame <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(E_i)$\">$(E_i)$</span>.  <p></p><section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ariemannian-density-pointwise\">↗ def:riemannian-density-pointwise</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Adensity-smooth\">↗ prop:density-smooth</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Adensity-transformation-law\">↗ prop:density-transformation-law</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Adensity-value-one\">↗ prop:density-value-one</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Adensity-uniqueness-pointwise\">↗ prop:density-uniqueness-pointwise</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Adensity-positive\">↗ prop:density-positive</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Aexistence-orthonormal-frames\">↗ prop:existence-orthonormal-frames</a> \\sketch Take the family of Definition <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ariemannian-density-pointwise\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-density-pointwise\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6465663a7269656d616e6e69616e2d64656e736974792d706f696e7477697365\">12.2</a>; Proposition <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Adensity-transformation-law\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:density-transformation-law\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-70726f703a64656e736974792d7472616e73666f726d6174696f6e2d6c6177\">9</a> makes each fibre a density and Proposition <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Adensity-smooth\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:density-smooth\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-70726f703a64656e736974792d736d6f6f7468\">12.2</a> makes the family smooth. Proposition <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Adensity-value-one\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:density-value-one\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-70726f703a64656e736974792d76616c75652d6f6e65\">9</a> gives (2.18) and positivity. For uniqueness, evaluate any competing density on a local orthonormal frame and apply Proposition <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Adensity-uniqueness-pointwise\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:density-uniqueness-pointwise\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-70726f703a64656e736974792d756e697175656e6573732d706f696e7477697365\">9</a> fibrewise. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:density-smooth","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:riemannian-density-formula","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-density","title":"def:smooth-density","label":"def:smooth-density"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-density-pointwise","title":"def:riemannian-density-pointwise","label":"def:riemannian-density-pointwise"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:density-smooth","title":"prop:density-smooth","label":"prop:density-smooth"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:density-transformation-law","title":"prop:density-transformation-law","label":"prop:density-transformation-law"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:density-value-one","title":"prop:density-value-one","label":"prop:density-value-one"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:density-uniqueness-pointwise","title":"prop:density-uniqueness-pointwise","label":"prop:density-uniqueness-pointwise"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:density-positive","title":"prop:density-positive","label":"prop:density-positive"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:existence-orthonormal-frames","title":"prop:existence-orthonormal-frames","label":"prop:existence-orthonormal-frames"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:riemannian-density-formula","title":"prop:riemannian-density-formula","label":"prop:riemannian-density-formula"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#exer:riemannian-density-formula","title":"exer:riemannian-density-formula","label":"exer:riemannian-density-formula"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:riemannian-density","title":"prop:riemannian-density","tex":"\\begin{proposition}[The Riemannian Density]\\label{prop:riemannian-density}\\dcref{ch2:2.44}\n\n\\uses{def:smooth-density, def:riemannian-density-pointwise, prop:density-smooth, prop:density-transformation-law, prop:density-value-one, prop:density-uniqueness-pointwise, prop:density-positive, prop:existence-orthonormal-frames}\n\n\n\n\nEvery Riemannian manifold has a unique smooth positive density $\\mu$ satisfying\n\\begin{equation}\n\\mu(E_1,\\ldots,E_n)=1 \\tag{2.18}\n\\end{equation}\nfor every local orthonormal frame $(E_i)$.\n\\end{proposition}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{def:riemannian-density-pointwise,prop:density-smooth,prop:density-transformation-law,prop:density-value-one,prop:density-uniqueness-pointwise,prop:density-positive,prop:existence-orthonormal-frames}\n\\sketch Take the family of Definition \\ref{def:riemannian-density-pointwise}; Proposition \\ref{prop:density-transformation-law} makes each fibre a density and Proposition \\ref{prop:density-smooth} makes the family smooth. Proposition \\ref{prop:density-value-one} gives (2.18) and positivity. For uniqueness, evaluate any competing density on a local orthonormal frame and apply Proposition \\ref{prop:density-uniqueness-pointwise} fibrewise.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-density","title":"def:smooth-density","des